Subject: [PATCH 02163/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE D1
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; harden
 .397) -- online verifier-weight adaptation with a POWERED CI in the
 cross-domain regime. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning
 experiment/milestone (Tier-1 = online counter updates, CPU, <1us/update).
 .397 (exp4295) showed online adaptation HELPS (online_cross_family_delta
 0.483 > static 0.417, +0.067; tier-2 fixed: memory 0.428, retrieval 0.456) --
 but reported the deltas WITHOUT a powered CI, so 'helps' is not yet
 decision-grade. HARDEN: re-run Tier-1 online reweighting + Tier-2
 RETRIEVAL-augmented selector-context (Decocted 2604.04373 / Dynamic
 Cheatsheet 2504.07952: retrieval-only CURATED context, NO weight mutation, NO
 LoRA) across the CROSS-DOMAIN family set (the .395 + exp4291 + the
 cross-domain pools, a soft input from exp4305) where distribution shift is
 larger -- and report a POWERED bootstrap CI95 (>=2000 resamples) on
 (best-adaptive - static). Emit online_adaptation_helps BARE bool :=
 (best-adaptive - static > 0 AND CI95-excl-0). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO
 fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA. A powered null (static is genuinely the
 ceiling, CI includes 0) RETIRES the online-adaptation ask
 (retire_if_same_verdict).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
