 - 2026-06-16: PHASE C1 (BROADEN the selection moat to cross-DOMAIN; the .397 SOTA-ingestion flag; new axis) -- a domain router + per-domain set-encoder that generalizes selection to a HELD-OUT DOMAIN. .397 CLOSED the cross-GENERATOR axis (exp4291 +0.50) -- but the moat is proven only WITHIN ARC, and the verifier is math-domain-bound (math strong, code weak, facts earned-negative). The .397 SOTA ingestion (exp4298) flagged: now that same-substrate cross-generator closed, BROADEN to cross-DOMAIN. Build a router over >=3 domains (ARC families + ARC-GEN generators [reuse exp4291's non-degenerate pool] + FoVer-step/math selection), train ONLY on train-DOMAIN outcomes, test beats-vote on a HELD-OUT DOMAIN frozen (EEVEE interleaved router-prompt co-evolution arXiv:2606.11182; DG-PRM multi-dimensional discriminators arXiv:2507.17849 = the selector-side route to OOD generalization). CRITICAL anti-leak (EEVEE's abstract does not detail leak prevention): a LABEL-ABLATION arm -- the router sees ONLY task features vs sees the domain/family label -- proving it is not just reading domain identity. Non-degenerate guards (vote@1>0.05, oracle<1.0, delta<0.95) so the new adversarial_verify DEGENERATE_SEPARATION check does not fire. Emit cross_domain_selection_holds BARE bool := (held-out-domain delta>0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND non-degenerate guards AND label_ablation_robust). verifier_is_oracle=false. A held-out-domain win is the strongest selection result yet (escapes the domain bound); a collapse is a genuine, decision-grade scope boundary. HARD-CAP to the window; an honest partial (>=3 domains, >=1 held-out, >=~12 held-out tasks) is fine. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: cross_domain_selection_collapses_domain_bound; results/experiment_4305_cross_domain_selector_generalization.json
